		{
			dependencies: ["6E91F39DD24C08A0"]
			id: "5F33B25DBD8CB512"
			rewards: [{
				id: "16361FBBF0317563"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					ForgeCaps: {
						"celestisynth:celestisynthitemstackcapabilities": {
							cs.aquaSkin: 0
						}
					}
					id: "minecraft:written_book"
					tag: {
						author: "Mr6trt"
						pages: [
							"{\"text\":\"They say the world was once fairer — not for its peace, but for its balance.\\nThe dwarves dug deep, as they always had, their songs echoing in tunnels carved by patient hands.\\n\\nThen came the Stone.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"It was not found in a vein or pried from rock. It was waiting, nestled in the heart of the mountains, glowing like a living ember beneath a throne of black slate.\\n\\nIt was said to breathe.\\nAnd with every breath, stone became treasure.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"Where its light touched, deepslate gave way to gold, granite to diamonds, cobble to emeralds. The dwarves called it Zaram-Nur, the Stone of Fortune.\\n\\nAnd their king, Alharn the Gilded, called it his.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"At first, the Stone was shared. Cities rose in days. Fortresses of silver and steel glimmered in the mountains. Gold flowed down rivers like rain. Even the elven courts bent knee in awe.\\n\\nBut the world saw what the Stone could do. And it wanted.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"War came swift. From the sky fell fire. From the Nether marched beasts of ash and bone.\\nThe other kings begged for shelter. They asked for aid, for steel, for walls.\\n\\nAlharn gave them silence.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"He sealed the gates of Khazrad-Kel, the golden palace.\\nHe turned his armies inward. He armed his sons and daughters with blades of gilded wrath.\\n\\n“Let the world burn,” he said. “The Stone is ours.”\\n\\nAnd burn it did.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"While the dwarves beneath the stone feasted on roasted apples dipped in gold, the overworld turned to shadow.\\n\\nOne by one, Alharn’s subjects grew pale. They whispered in the dark. They weighed friends against coins.\\nThey forgot the sun.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"The king adorned himself in golden armor shaped like the warriors of the East. He sat upon a throne of stacked emeralds, surrounded by rings of wealth and war.\\n\\nHe bathed in riches, yet dreamed only of betrayal.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"When the Nether breached the mountains, no help came. Alharn’s gates were sealed by his own hand. No dwarf escaped.\\n\\nAnd somewhere, beneath that ruined palace, the Stone still gleams.\\nWaiting.\\nListening.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"They say to find it, one must walk the forgotten halls of Alharn’s court.\\nWear his pride upon your chest — armor made of light and greed.\\nCarry his gluttony in both hands — apples dipped not once, but twice.\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"Bring tribute:\\nWhat he worshipped.\\nWhat he hoarded.\\nWhat cost him everything.\\n\\nOnly then, the Stone may awaken.\\nBut beware…\\n\\nThe final trial is a test of strength, against thoses who love Gold\"}"
							"{\"text\":\"The Stone of Fortune does not serve those who seek wealth.\\nIt consumes them.\\n\\n\"}"
						]
						title: "财富之石"
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
